## Swift 6 Strict Concurrency
- All `@Observable` classes → `@MainActor final class`
- Across-actor calls → `await` or `Task { @MainActor in }`
- No `DispatchQueue` — use structured concurrency

## SwiftUI Patterns
- `@Bindable var appModel: AppModel` — never `@StateObject` or `@ObservedObject`
- Local transient UI state only in `@State` (e.g., animation triggers, sheet visibility)
- No domain logic in view body — call engine methods

## Touch Targets (child UI)
- Minimum 80×80 pt interactive area
- Snap zones for drag-and-drop: 40–60 pt magnetic radius
- No timers, no buzzers, no red X — gentle self-correcting animations only

## Naming
- Views: `<Context>View`
- Engine actions: imperative verbs
- VS1-scoped UI: `VS1` prefix; app-wide: `Mather` prefix
